## Pioneer Standard-CAN findings\
\
### CAN ID `0x18D`\
\
| Bytes | Type and conversion | Proposed meaning | Pioneer evidence | Relation to externally supplied V2 data |\
|---|---|---|---|---|\
| `data[0]` | `uint8` | rolling counter or sequence | Covered nearly the full byte range during stable charging; not a direct measurement | Unknown |\
| `data[1..2]` | `int16`, little-endian | battery current; amperes = raw x 0.3 | Scale and sign confirmed during charging, traction and regeneration | Likely related, but the V2 source does not expose an unambiguous raw-ID association |\
| `data[3..4]` | `uint16`, little-endian mV | HV pack voltage | Confirmed by MOT | Same mapping was supplied, but it fails on the tested large-battery vehicle |\
| `data[5]` | `uint8` | unknown | Stable `0x00` in recorded phases | Unknown |\
| `data[6]` | `uint8` state | `0x10` unplugged; `0x20` plugged | Confirmed by repeated powered and AC-deenergized plug tests; transient `0x04` also occurred | V2 source calls it a charge/status byte |\
| `data[7]` | `uint8` | Standard/BMS SOC candidate | Raw value confirmed; stayed 90 while Pioneer display showed 97\'96100% | Same byte was supplied as Display SOC; large-battery live value `0x05` remains uninterpreted |\
\
### Charging evidence for `0x18D data[1..2]`\
\
| Vehicle/charger state | Signed raw | Pack voltage | External measurement | Interpretation |\
|---|---:|---:|---:|---|\
| Awake, unplugged | about -4 | about 53.0 V | 0 W | Idle offset |\
| Plugged, EVSE AC-side off | about -4 | about 53.0 V | 0 W | Plugged but not charging |\
| Stable charge | 112\'96118 | about 53.3 V | 1,836 W gross AC input | `115 \'d7 0.3 A \'d7 53.3 V \uc0\u8776  1,839 W` |\
| Taper charge at 98\'9699% display SOC | 43\'9647 | about 53.2 V | 762 W gross AC input | `45 \'d7 0.3 A \'d7 53.2 V \uc0\u8776  718 W` before conversion losses |\
| External AC removed, cable retained | about -4 | falling from charge voltage | 0 W | Charging stopped, still plugged |\
| Natural completion at 100% display SOC | fell from +45 to -3 | about 53.24 V at end | Fell from 762 W to 0 W | Stable post-charge idle offset |\
\
Lower-SOC measurements at several charge settings confirmed 0.3 A per raw unit.\
At about 50 V, the derived DC values tracked independent 1,809 W, 2,088 W and\
approximately 2,340 W references within expected conversion and vehicle-load\
differences. Three controlled road captures then confirmed negative current during\
traction and positive current during regeneration. Observed results included about\
4.8 kW pedal-release regeneration, 7.8 kW with light braking and a later normal-\
road peak of about 20.9 kW discharge.\
\
### CAN ID `0x4AD`\
\
| Bytes | Type and conversion | Proposed meaning | Status |\
|---|---|---|---|\
| `data[0..1]` | `uint16`, little-endian mV | cell value A | Plausible on Pioneer; externally supplied under an unresolved V2 label |\
| `data[2..3]` | `uint16`, little-endian mV | cell value B | Plausible on Pioneer; externally supplied under an unresolved V2 label |\
| derived | `min(A, B)` | minimum cell value | Plausible |\
| derived | `max(A, B)` | maximum cell value | Plausible |\
| derived | `max(A, B) - min(A, B)` | cell delta | Plausible |\
\
Stable examples included 4,081/4,078 mV before charging and approximately\
4,105/4,100 mV during charge. Larger transient divergence occurred around charge\
start, so the exact semantics must remain provisional until repeated captures\
exclude multiplexing or transition-specific payload use.\
\
## Newer Microlino with large battery\
\
A live Standard-CAN capture from a newer Microlino with the approximately\
200-240 km battery received hundreds of thousands of CAN1 frames without bus\
errors. `0x18D` was present continuously, while `0x4AD` was absent. One stable\
`0x18D` payload was:\
\
`01 02 11 18 03 00 03 05`\
\
Applying the Pioneer layout would produce 1,306.2 A, 792 mV pack voltage, status\
`0x03` and an SOC candidate of 5%. The current and voltage results are physically\
impossible, proving that the Pioneer byte layout cannot be used for this vehicle.\
The frame must remain raw discovery data until controlled unplugged, plugged,\
charging, traction and regeneration captures identify the actual signals.\
\
The earlier source may have been recorded from a Pioneer/V1 vehicle, or from a\
newer Microlino whose medium battery and BMS retain the Pioneer layout. This is a\
working hypothesis only: the source does not document the exact vehicle, battery\
or BMS generation. The name `V2` must therefore not be treated as a single CAN\
protocol generation.\
\
### Confirmed large-battery BMS layout\
\
The recovered original PID workbook and Flespi configuration identify a separate\
big-endian layout. A 16,675-frame capture from the large-battery vehicle contains\
all three IDs with matching physically plausible values:\
\
| CAN ID | Direct bus decoding | Captured evidence | Decoder status |\
|---:|---|---|---|\
| `0x1B0` | bytes 2-3 pack mV, 4-5 minimum cell mV, 6-7 maximum cell mV; big-endian | 47,317-47,326 mV pack and 3,635-3,643 mV cells | Implemented |\
| `0x1B1` | bytes 0-1 SOC x100, bytes 2-3 SOH x100; big-endian | 32.15% SOC and 97.01% SOH | Implemented as BMS-specific values |\
| `0x2BA` | bytes 0-1 signed big-endian current x10 | stationary -1.9 to -2.1 A | Implemented; sign still needs drive/charge confirmation |\
\
The direct CAN order must be used by MOT. The Flespi `manual.can.hex.*` conversion\
reverses groups of 16-bit words internally and must not be copied as bus byte\
order. Pack power is derived only when fresh `0x1B0` voltage and plausible\
`0x2BA` current are available. Plugged and active charging remain unknown. AWS\
continues to publish Display-CAN `0x602` as `display/soc`; BMS SOC is kept\
separate and never overwrites the confirmed display value.\
\
